A||||3||Ed||Windows, electric, short stopped||||5||
Z||000000||Ed||02-22-2000||09:39 PM||||My power window on the driver's side has gotten lazy. On occasion it only goes up about three inches from the full down position. I have a shop manual so I can check the circuits, but does anyone have a quick diagnosis? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||sdm1964||02-22-2000||09:42 PM||||I have heard that the grease gets hard, makes them slow, sounds like yours might be a good canidate, i heard it is worse when cold.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||02-22-2000||09:53 PM||||No, I'm in warm Calif! The window doesn't slow down, it just flat out stops as if there's a failure in the limiter. I can't hear any noises, clunks, etc. I keep trying and it starts up again. So I've got an intermittant failure, the best kind to diagnose (Ha!).   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||b_b_a_d||02-23-2000||01:39 AM||||Well, I just pulled the switches out of my 86 w/power windows because the passenger side wasn't working at all.  It seems the previous owner has dumped a few pops on the console over the years.  The soda pop and all the dog hair (don't ask) got in the switch and was keeping the contact points from making there conection.  I pulled off the top of the switch and the spring and took a little electronics screwdriver to move the contact points back and forth while soaking it in some hot water.  You should have seen all the dirt and grime that was coming out of this thing.  Anyway, dried it off and now all works just like new!!!  You sound like you have a different problem, but it is worth a shot if it is intermittent.<p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 02-23-2000).]||||reg||6
